does your solution scan the data? If the library had 100,000 borrow records, would your approach still be practical? Can you think of away that requires 
fewer passes?
Problem faced :
-->At first, I did not understand how to find the books that were borrowed more than one time.
-->It was difficult to make sure the same book ID is not printed again and again.
-->I had to think about how to check every book without missing any.
-->I realized that checking every book with every other book can take more time.

